troski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.03622871964046319,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":18.1,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.1987092799030177,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":66.9,"_gate_incr_roic":0.11038625087865454,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":53.5,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.0642166496615467,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":54.7,"_gate_pool_share":-0.04129378987586141,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":23.5,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.125790074902985,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":87.9,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.05195355250267737,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":68.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0017560956081099643,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":47.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.007622471511357885,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":87.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.00467,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.5,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":50.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Mid-America Apartment Communities, Inc. is a real estate investment trust (REIT) focused on delivering full-cycle and superior investment performance for shareholders through the ownership, management, acquisition, development and redevelopment of quality apartment communities primarily in the Southeast, Southwest and Mid-Atlantic regions of the United States. As of September 30, 2026, MAA had ownership interest in 105,136 apartment units, including communities in development, across 16 states and the District of Columbia. Mid-America Apartment Communities, Inc. was incorporated in 1977 in Tennessee and is based in Germantown, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Adrian Bradley Hill C.F.A. | CEO, President & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $881K ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $286K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Mid-America Apartment Communiti is a large-cap real estate business with a $14.1B market cap on $2.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 8% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $718M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 32 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.41\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 3.5\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 22% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","31 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Real Estate peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Lowered Earnings Guidance Will Impact MAA Stock Investors","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-maa/mid-america-apartment-communities/news/how-lowered-earnings-guidance-will-impact-maa-stock-investor","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793928580.347,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Recent Research Analysts\u2019 Ratings Updates for Mid-America Apartment Communities (MAA)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianon